{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:NuclearInteractions.NEquals1VacuousMagic","@type":"LeanModule","name":"NuclearInteractions.NEquals1VacuousMagic","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.one_isAlgebraicallyPrime","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.one_isAlgebraicallyPrime","kind":"theorem","line":15,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/n-equals-1-vacuous-magic.lean#L15-L23","doc":"**Re-export.** For every `q : ℝ`, the integer `n = 1` is\nalgebraically prime — proved via vacuous truth on the empty\nset of valid decompositions. See\n`QOU.Interactions.AlgebraicPrimality.one_isAlgebraicallyPrime`\nfor the proof. ","signatureChunk":0}]}